    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. We also need to monitor our storage areas for any signs of contamination or unexpected spoilage that might happen if the cooling process fails. What are the most common visual or olfactory indicators that a batch has started to go bad due to improper temperature control?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common visual indicators include off-colors, slime or sliminess on the surface, or visible mold growth on the poultry. Olfactorily, a sour, pungent, or distinctly \"off\" odor is a strong sign of spoilage, regardless of the temperature. Any unusual texture change, such as becoming excessively mushy or dry, can also signal bacterial activity. If you notice any combination of these signs, the batch must be discarded immediately.",
      "source": "target",
